# Bug report

**Reproduction Steps**

See https://github.com/kelunik/webpack-5-testing/commit/a800896c6c10df3572d50b573ef03c9e2a8607f6 for a simple reproduction. The README includes two scenarios, both for the large file and generic tracking of the project root as build dependency.

**What is the current behavior?**

```
<w> [webpack.cache.PackFileCacheStrategy] Caching failed for pack: Error: Unable to snapshot build dependencies
```

I did some debugging in `FileSystemInfo.js` and found the following error here: 

```
this._getContextTimestampAndHash(path, (err, entry) => {
	if (err) {
		if (this.logger) {
			this.logger.debug(
				`Error snapshotting context timestamp hash combination of ${path}: ${err}`
			);
		}
		jobError();
	} else {
		contextTshs.set(path, entry);
		jobDone();
	}
});
```

```
RangeError [ERR_FS_FILE_TOO_LARGE]: File size (3458767214) is greater than possible Buffer: 2147483647 bytes
    at FSReqCallback.readFileAfterStat [as oncomplete] (fs.js:278:11) {
  code: 'ERR_FS_FILE_TOO_LARGE'
}
```

**What is the expected behavior?**

I'm not sure, but the current error message neither says what the actual error is nor how to work around such a problem. I'm not sure whether the problem itself can be avoided. Maybe users running into this need to apply filters to the context?

**Other relevant information:**
webpack version:  5.3.2
Node.js version: 12.16.3
Operating System: Ubuntu / Linux
